<section aria-label="Detail document">

  <h2 id="structural-context" class="section-title">Structural Context</h2>
  <p><b>Why 75% of qualified candidates never get interviewed</b> in high-volume environments: evaluation bandwidth is the constraint, not applicant supply.</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <b>Core constraint</b><br>
    A single open role can receive 800–1,000 applications. Even if only 10% are viable, that still produces 80–100 candidates requiring thoughtful evaluation — but recruiter and hiring manager interview capacity rarely scales at the same rate.
  </div>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="operator-origin" class="section-title">Operator Origin</h2>
  <p>From manual craft (competitor mapping, tenure analysis, employer context research, calibration training) to scalable infrastructure.</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="research-validation" class="section-title">Research &amp; External Validation</h2>
  <p>Evidence that time pressure increases heuristic decision-making, and structured methods outperform unstructured evaluation — plus market signals (AI-driven inbound volume, candidate trust erosion, vendor risk).</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="problem-definition" class="section-title">Problem Definition</h2>
  <p>When inbound application volume exceeds evaluation bandwidth, qualified candidates fail to reach consistent, structured review, increasing bias risk under pressure and reducing transparency in hiring outcomes.</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="strategy" class="section-title">Strategy</h2>
  <p><b>Goal:</b> Ensure consistent, structured evaluation of inbound applications while preserving recruiter judgment and decision authority.</p>
  <p><b>North Star Metric:</b> % of inbound applications receiving structured, documented screening evaluation within 48 hours of receipt.</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <b>Intervention model</b><br>
    Inputs → Rubric assembly → Evidence extraction → Hybrid scoring → Recommendation → Structured ATS writeback.
  </div>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="system-architecture" class="section-title">System Architecture</h2>
  <p>Rubric-first evaluation, hybrid scoring (bands + numeric), risk flags as moderated penalties, ask-next prompts, and ATS writeback fields.</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="governance-guardrails" class="section-title">Governance &amp; Guardrails</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No fully automated rejection — a human must confirm “Do Not Advance.”</li>
    <li>Overrides require short documented rationale.</li>
    <li>Rubrics and weights are documented and discoverable by TA &amp; hiring managers.</li>
    <li>The agent does not infer or store protected characteristic data.</li>
    <li>All scoring categories map to explicit job-relevant criteria.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="mvp-scope" class="section-title">MVP Scope</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>JD → structured rubric generator</li>
    <li>Resume signal extraction (experience depth, tenure, employer mapping, skills alignment)</li>
    <li>Hybrid band + numeric scoring</li>
    <li>Recommendation engine</li>
    <li>Ask-next recruiter prompts</li>
    <li>ATS field mapping + writeback</li>
    <li>Override tracking for calibration</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">This scope prioritizes evaluation consistency and auditability over predictive modeling.</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="rollout-model" class="section-title">Rollout Model</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Shadow mode (1–2 weeks)</b>: generate outputs without changing decisions; compare agent outputs to recruiter outcomes.</li>
    <li><b>Human-confirm mode (2–4 weeks)</b>: recruiter reviews recommendation and must confirm/override.</li>
    <li><b>Governance loop (ongoing)</b>: quarterly rubric reviews + override analysis + fairness monitoring.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="measurement-tracking" class="section-title">Measurement &amp; Tracking</h2>
  <p><b>Primary metric:</b> Application Screening Completion Rate (48h).</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Time from application received → screening decision</li>
    <li>Override rate + direction (Advance ↔ Do Not Advance)</li>
    <li>Application → recruiter screen conversion (by source/role)</li>
    <li>Application → HM interview conversion (capacity-adjusted)</li>
    <li>False negatives sampling (audit set)</li>
    <li>Candidate experience proxy: response-time SLA adherence</li>
    <li>Downstream correlation (Strong/Solid → interview/offer)</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <h2 id="limitations" class="section-title">Limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>I’d validate rubric weights with role-specific calibration workshops earlier (reduce early override spikes).</li>
    <li>I’d run audit sampling for “Do Not Advance” to estimate false negatives without adding workload.</li>
    <li>I’d pair candidate sentiment surveys with SLA + transparency metrics.</li>
    <li>I intentionally excluded automated interviews and sourcing workflows to keep the MVP focused and governable.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="rule"></div>

